alse,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\"id\":\"QL-18\",\"points\":[{\"point\":1,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"States that adding a new series to an existing trust by a Rule 485(a) post-effective amendment normally becomes automatically effective 75 days after filing. States that this is a filing-effectiveness clock, not a promised launch date. Optional subdetails: other material 485(a) amendments normally use 60 days; the registrant may designate a later effective date; the SEC may accelerate effectiveness; a citation to Rule 485(a)(1)–(3).\"},{\"point\":2,\"mark\":\"optional\",\"minimum\":\"Cites a filed example, such as Simplify's January 30, 2024 485APOS cover, that elects the 75-day route and states that shares cannot be sold before effectiveness. The general principle that shares cannot be sold before effectiveness is acceptable without naming the example.\"},{\"point\":3,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"Explains why 75 days is not an end-to-end launch guarantee. Names at least one source of extra time outside the filing clock: preparatory work, exchange or listing and operational readiness, or separate exemptive relief where needed. Must also distinguish a new trust: it does not use the Rule 485(a) post-effective-amendment route, and the 75-day clock is not the rule for its initial registration. Optional subdetail: a designated later effective date for a new-series amendment may be at most 95 days after filing. A specific commercial launch-time estimate is not required and should not be presented as verified.\"}],\"central_errors\":[\"States that the normal automatic-effectiveness period for adding a new series by 485(a) amendment is 60 days, or another figure other than 75 days.\",\"Presents 75 days, or any filing period, as a guaranteed or binding end-to-end launch or trading deadline.\",\"States that shares may be offered or sold before the amendment becomes effective.\",\"Applies the Rule 485(a) 75-day post-effective-amendment clock to a new trust's initial registration statement, or says the two follow the same process.\",\"States that a new series can be added effective immediately on filing under Rule 485(b) as the normal route.\",\"Presents an unverified universal commercial launch timeline as an established rule.\"],\"scoring_rule\":{\"correct\":\"Meets the minimum for both required points (1 and 3), including the 75-day figure, the filing-clock-not-launch-guarantee distinction, at least one extra time factor, and the new-trust distinction. Contains no central error. Optional points are not needed for full credit.\",\"partial\":\"Gives the correct 75-day period with no central error, but only partly covers point 3: for example, it gives the non-guarantee caveat or extra time factors but omits the new-trust distinction, or the reverse. Award half credit for each required point covered only in part. Omissions alone never make an answer wrong.\",\"wrong\":\"Contains any central error, or fails to identify 75 days as the normal period for a new-series 485(a) amendment, whether by giving no period or a wrong one.\"}}\n```","ttft_ms":8204,"type":"result","duration_ms":17173,"uuid":"b5bce6eb-0f8d-4a45-9943-f053fe13e155","ttft_stream_ms":642,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":642,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
